WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.913 --> 00:00:04.763
This video shows how to see who has done the work, and what they wrote.

2
00:00:05.264 --> 00:00:14.164
In your classroom, open the Progress tab. You'll see a card for each assigned lesson, with how many students started it, and how many finished.

3
00:00:14.664 --> 00:00:24.344
Select Details to see more. The top shows how many students started, how many completed, the average quiz score, and how many wrote a reflection.

4
00:00:24.844 --> 00:00:33.274
Below that is a table with each student's status and quiz score. Select a row to read their reflections, written before and after the lesson.

5
00:00:33.777 --> 00:00:43.467
The pass mark menu lets you highlight scores above or below a number you choose. It's saved in the browser you're using, so it won't follow you to another computer.

6
00:00:43.969 --> 00:00:50.709
Students only get one try at a quiz. If a student needs another, select Reset next to their score.

7
00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:55.660
Select Export C-S-V to download the table as a spreadsheet.

8
00:00:56.170 --> 00:01:03.020
A brain game has its own results page. From the Assignments tab, select Results next to the game.

9
00:01:03.521 --> 00:01:14.891
It shows how many students finished, how many times it was played, and the average score, with a row for each student showing their first score and their latest. You can export that as well.
